From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] server: a new shell takes over the desktop window a dead one left

When the shell died while programs kept the desktop alive (a crash kept by
its debugger, a tray program), its desktop window lived on with no thread.
The shell started again got a window made a child of that one; its
WM_NCCREATE refused it and the shell exited, as every restart did: no
desktop and no taskbar until the person signed out (David 2026-10-01,
after AmbirScan crashed the desktop; 0755 fixed the X side of it).

Now the next desktop-class window made on that desktop is the detached
window itself, owned again by the new shell's thread: its handle, which
every program has, stays, as do the programs' windows on it. win32u
accepts the handle it already knew as the desktop.

Gate: test/shellrestart-gate.sh (mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_DESKTOP_TAKEOVER and
SG_MUTANT_STALE_DESKTOP fail it).
---
--- a/server/window.c
+++ b/server/window.c
@@ -631,6 +631,32 @@
 
     if (!parent)  /* null parent is only allowed for desktop or HWND_MESSAGE top window */
     {
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_NO_DESKTOP_TAKEOVER
+        /* Stained Glass: a desktop window no thread owns any more -- its shell
+         * died while programs kept the desktop alive (or it was made by
+         * get_desktop_window before the shell came) -- is taken over by the
+         * shell that creates the desktop next, keeping its handle and the
+         * programs' windows on it. It became a child of that window instead,
+         * the shell's WM_NCCREATE refused that, and every restarted shell
+         * exited: no desktop until the person signed out. */
+        if (is_desktop_class( class ) && (win = desktop->top_window) && !win->thread)
+        {
+            if (!current->queue && !init_thread_queue( current ))
+            {
+                win = NULL;
+                goto failed;
+            }
+            win->thread  = current;
+            win->class   = class;  /* the reference grab_class took */
+            win->desktop = desktop;  /* and get_thread_desktop's */
+            win->owner   = owner ? owner->handle : 0;
+            win->paint_flags &= ~PAINT_INTERNAL;
+            if (win->update_region) inc_queue_paint_count( current, 1 );
+            set_process_default_desktop( current->process, desktop, current->desktop );
+            current->desktop_users++;
+            return win;
+        }
+#endif
         if (is_desktop_class( class ))
             parent = desktop->top_window;  /* use existing desktop if any */
         else if (is_hwnd_message_class( class ))
--- a/dlls/win32u/window.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/window.c
@@ -5584,7 +5584,10 @@
         if (name->Buffer == (const WCHAR *)DESKTOP_CLASS_ATOM)
         {
             if (!thread_info->top_window) thread_info->top_window = HandleToUlong( full_parent ? full_parent : handle );
-            else assert( full_parent == UlongToHandle( thread_info->top_window ));
+            /* or the server gave this thread the desktop window no thread
+             * owned any more (its shell died): the handle it had already */
+            else assert( full_parent == UlongToHandle( thread_info->top_window ) ||
+                         (!full_parent && handle == UlongToHandle( thread_info->top_window )));
             if (!thread_info->top_window) ERR_(win)( "failed to create desktop window\n" );
             else user_driver->pSetDesktopWindow( UlongToHandle( thread_info->top_window ));
             register_builtin_classes();
